      "mergedPostDetails": "Saw older posts discussing this, but not recently. Most discuss uncapping FPS through launch options or the like.\n\nWith the ability to uncap now part of VRChat proper, it is now more pertinent to get attention drawn to this. \n\nBuild version: 1296\n\n1. Open VRChat in DESKTOP MODE specifically.\n\n2. Go to Settings-> Graphics Tab-> \"Common\"-> FPS Cap-> Set to \"Unlimited\"\n\n3. Attempt to move your mouse. Vertical movement seems to be fine, but horizontal is SEVERELY decreased.\n\nExtra: Depending on if your monitor supports higher FPS values (120, 144, etc.), you may even see this on \"VSYNC\" mode, as the bug seems to be tied to framerate.\n\nI see mention of what *could* be causing it in multiple Canny's mentioning \"Time.deltaTime\". I have two here, one is from 2020, the other from 2022. I'm not... all that technical, so I'll just put them in this post.\n\n2020 - https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/1010-horizontal-mouse-input-dont-use-timedeltatime\n\n2022 - https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/bug-pc-horizontal-mouse-movent-is-not-scaled\n\nEdit: I searched high and low for one, but perhaps I'm not using the right search terms. If there is a canny post for this particular issue, by all means direct me. Everything I found was *mostly* old.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Setting FPS to \"Unlimited\" slows horizontal mouse Speed.",
